Value release (.*)
Value hostname (.*)
Value management_vlan (.*)
Value primary_vlan (.*)

# Parse the output of "show running-config" on an HP AOS-S switch.
#
# The running config is a nested block structure, not a table, so this
# template is deliberately minimal: it captures the software release from
# the header comment line, the device hostname from the hostname
# statement, the management VLAN from the management-vlan statement, and
# the primary VLAN from the primary-vlan statement.
# Nested blocks (vlan, interface, ip route, password manager) are not
# parsed here.
#
# No rule uses -> Record: gotextfsm emits the single record at EOF, so
# every captured field lands in the same record regardless of the order
# the statements appear in.


Start
  ^; .*Created on release #(?P<release>YA\.[\d.]+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^hostname "(?P<hostname>\S+)"\s*$ -> Continue
  ^management-vlan (?P<management_vlan>\d+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^primary-vlan (?P<primary_vlan>\d+)\s*$ -> Continue
